  "summaries": {
    "en": "Resource routing, Duke upgrade priority, and boss strategies for all four lords in Resident Evil Village.",
    "ja": "リソースルーティング、デュークアップグレードの優先度、村の4貴族全員のボス戦略を解説するバイオハザード ヴィレッジ攻略ガイド。"
  },
  "category": "survival-horror",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551269901-5c3b16b12d30?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "The Duke's Kitchen (cooking upgrades) provides permanent stat boosts that stack—prioritise the Animal Health dish (HP +20 per cook) and Poultry with Citrus Herbs (Defensive Bonus +20%) over weapon upgrades in the first two lords' areas.",
      "Selling treasure items to the Duke increases his shop stock—complete the combination treasures (Crimson Skull, Cesare's Goblet) before selling for the highest combined value, which funds early shotgun upgrades.",
      "In Lady Dimitrescu's Castle, weapon ammo is scarce—conserve pistol ammo for daughters (the weaker mini-bosses) and use pipe bombs exclusively against Lady D herself to stagger her without spending firearm ammo.",
      "The four lord areas can be completed in the recommended order or revisited after obtaining specific items—the Mold area (Moreau) provides the Crank item that unlocks shortcuts in the Village and Beneviento's House areas, so prioritising it second saves total backtrack time.",
      "Infinite ammo weapons (unlocked after completing NG+) transform subsequent playthroughs but are only accessible in NG+ mode—first playthrough always uses standard ammo economy."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "デュークのキッチン（料理アップグレード）は積み重なる永続的なステータスブーストを提供する。最初の2人の貴族エリアでは、武器アップグレードよりも動物の健康の料理（HPは料理ごとに+20）と柑橘ハーブ入りポーチドエッグ（防御ボーナス+20%）を優先する。",
      "デュークへのトレジャーアイテムの売却は彼のショップストックを増加させる。最高の複合価値のために売却前にコンビネーショントレジャー（クリムゾンスカル、チェザーレのゴブレット）を完成させる。これが序盤のショットガンアップグレードに資金を提供する。",
      "ディミトレスク夫人の城では武器の弾薬が不足している。娘たち（より弱いミニボス）のためにピストルの弾薬を節約し、銃器の弾薬を使わずにスタッガーさせるために夫人本人専用にパイプ爆弾を使う。",
      "4人の貴族エリアは推奨される順序で完了するか、特定のアイテムを取得した後に再訪できる。カビエリア（モロー）は村とベネヴィエントの家エリアのショートカットをロック解除するクランクアイテムを提供する。2番目に優先することで総バックトラック時間を節約できる。",
      "無限弾薬武器（NG+完了後にロック解除）は後続のプレイスルーを変えるが、NG+モードでのみアクセス可能。初回プレイスルーは常に標準の弾薬経済を使用する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Village Opening Resource Collection",
        "body": "The Village section (Act 1) has the highest resource density relative to threat level in the game. Collect all resources before entering any lord's domain: Herb patches in Village East, Livestock resources from the farm animals roaming freely, and the hidden Crimson Skull treasure in the Ceremony Site drawer. These resources, combined with treasure sales, provide enough Lei to purchase the Shotgun from the Duke's first encounter—the Shotgun is the most versatile defensive weapon for the Castle (Dimitrescu) area."
      },
      {
        "title": "Dimitrescu Castle Strategy",
        "body": "The Castle is a multi-floor maze with three optional treasures in locked rooms (requiring key items to unlock) and three mandatory boss encounters (the daughters). Daughters are killed by their elemental weakness: Cassandra (ice)—use Flashbang then shoot, Daniela (fire)—use Grenade then shoot, Bela (cold)—use Flashbang. Each daughter drops 5,000+ Lei in items, funding mid-Castle upgrades. Lady Dimitrescu is defeated by exposing her weakness to cold (Crispin's statue—the puzzle in the Opera Hall triggers the phase change window)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Beneviento House: No-Combat Section",
        "body": "Beneviento's House (Lord Beneviento area) is a pure puzzle/horror section with no combat. The puzzle solution sequence: 1) find the music box and winding key, 2) use the ring from the mannequin to open the music box lid, 3) solve the music box puzzle by ear (match the note sequence), 4) obtain the film negatives from the development room and solve the clock puzzle. The baby encounter in the basement requires hiding under beds during the approach phase—never run in the basement as the sound triggers the attack AI instantly."
      },
      {
        "title": "Moreau and Heisenberg Area Transition",
        "body": "The Moreau (fish lord) fight is simplest of the four lords—equip the Shotgun and Grenade Launcher (bought from Duke after Castle) and target his exposed weak point whenever the fish-form surfaces. After Moreau, Heisenberg's Factory (industrial area) introduces Soldat enemies with armoured variants that require hitting exposed components. Maintain Sniper Rifle ammo from the Duke specifically for the Stronghold section where Soldat Panzer variants require two sniper shots to expose their core."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Miranda and NG+ Planning",
        "body": "Mother Miranda is the final boss with three phases. Phase 1 (humanoid): target the exposed core during her wing-shield gaps. Phase 2 (insect): maintain distance and use Rocket Launcher charges during the stationary phase. Phase 3 (mutated): target the core with Magnum shots—stockpile 5+ Magnum rounds before entering the final sequence. After completion, Wolfsbane Magnum (free on NG+), the STAKE (Magnum), and unlocked weapons transform subsequent difficulty challenges. The highest challenge is Village of Shadows difficulty where every enemy has triple HP."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Using ammo recklessly in the Village section—the first hour's ammo stock determines available upgrades; conserve by kicking Lycan enemies that are staggered rather than shooting them at point-blank range.",
      "Selling all ingredients before cooking all available recipes—Duke's Kitchen recipes require fresh procurement of animal parts; selling before cooking removes the stat bonus opportunity permanently for that playthrough.",
      "Fighting Urias (giant troll in Village) head-on—Urias requires 3 Pipe Bombs and 10+ Shotgun shots; running past him to the gate is faster and conserves ammo for Castle lords.",
      "Not collecting the Wooden Animal puzzle pieces—the four Wooden Animals scattered across the Village combine into a treasure worth 6,000 Lei; this is the most valuable single-sell item available before the Castle and is easily missed.",
      "Entering Heisenberg's Factory without the Grenade Launcher—the Factory introduces armoured enemies that require explosive damage to reveal weak points; entering with only pistol and shotgun means wasting 2× ammo on each armoured enemy."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "村セクションで無造作に弾薬を使う。最初の1時間の弾薬ストックが利用可能なアップグレードを決定する。スタッガーしたライカン敵を接近で射撃するのではなくキックして節約する。",
      "全ての料理レシピを調理する前に全ての食材を売る。デュークのキッチンレシピは新鮮な動物パーツの調達が必要。調理前に売ると、そのプレイスルーのステータスボーナスの機会が永久に失われる。",
      "ウリアス（村の巨大トロル）に正面から立ち向かう。ウリアスはパイプ爆弾3個とショットガン10+発が必要。門に向かって走り抜けることでより速く、城の貴族のための弾薬を節約できる。",
      "木製動物のパズルピースを収集しない。村全体に散らばっている4体の木製動物は6,000レイの価値があるトレジャーに組み合わされる。これは城の前に利用可能な最も価値ある単品売りアイテムで、容易に見逃せる。",
      "グレネードランチャーなしでハイゼンベルクの工場に入る。工場は弱点を露わにするために爆発ダメージを必要とする装甲敵を導入する。ピストルとショットガンのみで入ると、各装甲敵に2倍の弾薬を無駄にすることになる。"
    ]
  },
